Fixing Grub 
===========

Note:-  
"""
	Windows boot loader 
	Windows boot manager

Windows boot loader:-
===================

 	Windows Boot Loader actually loads the operating system's kernel into memory

Windows boot manager:-
====================
		
	Windows Boot Manager handles the selection menu and overall boot configuration
"""

fdisk -l --> (list all the avaiable partition's on the system

mount  /mnt/sda1 /mnt/boot/efi --> (It mount's the efi partition that is associated with window boot loader)

mount  /mnt/nvem0n1p1 /mnt --> Just change in the parition name 

mount  /mnt/sda4 /mnt/ --> The ext4 file-system associated with dual booting of linux operating system

for i in /dev /dev/pts /sys /run do; mount -B $i /mnt$i; done 

				or

for i in /dev /dev/pts /sys /run do; mount --bind $i /mnt$i; done


chroot /mnt --> chroot is used to change the root directory to changed one

grub-install /dev/sdb | /dev/nvme0n1p

mount -t efivarfs none /sys/firmware/efi/efivars

update-grub

efibootmgr --> Used to verify the EFI boot order and confirm the new ubuntu/linux entry was created successfully



